# tools/al/ales_halve_neg_witness.rish — the inverted half-wave rectifier: keep the negative half, zero the positive, y = min(x, 0) (ALES86).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES86.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-214941_fill-ales86-lotus-inverted-half-wave-rectifier.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max). The half-wave rectifier (ALES85) keeps the POSITIVE half (y = max(x, 0)); this rung
# is its mirror — it keeps the NEGATIVE half (y = min(x, 0)). Together the two half-waves PARTITION the wave: max(x, 0) + min(x, 0) = x. A keeper who
# wants the two halves separately runs ALES85's halve and this halve_neg over the same span — both in-place maps whose outputs sum back to the dry wave.
#
# lotus/halve_neg.rye maps each sample to min(x, 0) — the negative half kept whole, the positive half silenced. The crux mirrors ALES85's: min(x, 0) is
# EXACT for EVERY i16 with NO rail edge, so NO saturate is needed, and sample_min passes THROUGH untouched (unlike the full-wave rectifier, where its
# magnitude overflowed the positive rail). Harmonically it is the even+odd mix sign-flipped: min(x, 0) = (x − |x|) / 2 carries the fundamental plus even
# harmonics minus a DC term. The map is MEMORYLESS, IDEMPOTENT (a non-positive sample maps to itself), and always NON-POSITIVE. The selftest proves it:
# non-positives pass unchanged; positives fold to silence (1→0, 100→0, 12345→0, 32767→0); there is no rail edge (sample_min passes, sample_max silences);
# every output is non-positive and the map is idempotent; the two half-waves partition the wave (halve + halve_neg = the dry wave, sample for sample);
# the span discipline holds; a span past the end refuses BadRange (min(x, 0) has no illegal parameter), the clip untouched. Purely local — one
# compare-and-keep per sample; no gain, no ceiling, no threshold, no saturate, no delay line, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no real
# device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_halve_neg_witness.rish

say "ales-halve-neg: Language EN — the half-wave rectifier (ALES85) keeps the POSITIVE half of the wave and silences the negative (y = max(x, 0)). This rung is its mirror: it keeps the NEGATIVE half and silences the positive — y = min(x, 0). A single diode oriented one way passes the positive half; flip the diode and it passes the negative half. Together the two half-wave rectifiers PARTITION the wave: max(x, 0) + min(x, 0) = x, the plainest decomposition of a signal into its positive and negative parts."
say "ales-halve-neg: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: the negative half of the wave is kept WHOLE, the positive half SILENCED. The crux mirrors ALES85's — min(x, 0) is EXACT for EVERY i16 with NO rail edge: a non-positive sample passes unchanged, a positive sample becomes 0, and NO saturate is needed; sample_min passes THROUGH untouched (unlike the full-wave rectifier, where its magnitude 32768 overflowed the positive rail). Harmonically it is the even+odd mix sign-flipped — min(x, 0) = (x − |x|) / 2 carries the fundamental plus the even harmonics minus a DC term. The map is MEMORYLESS, IDEMPOTENT, and always NON-POSITIVE."
say "ales-halve-neg: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM inverted-half-wave-rectified in place over a span; y = (if x < 0 then x else 0) with no wide intermediate and no saturate (min(x, 0) never leaves [sample_min, 0]); the map is memoryless (every output depends only on its own input); a span outside the samples refuses BadRange before any write, the clip untouched on refusal, and no other fault exists (min(x, 0) has no illegal parameter); siloed to lotus/, no gain, no ceiling, no threshold, no saturate, no delay line, no anti-aliasing, no snapshot, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/halve_neg"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/halve_neg.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-halve-neg: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/halve_neg.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-halve-neg: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-halve-neg: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-halve-neg' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-halve-neg: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-halve-neg line"
